WEBVTT

00:00:21.460 --> 00:00:23.750
How is it?

00:00:25.210 --> 00:00:26.710
I think it's great.

00:00:28.100 --> 00:00:29.740
Thank you.

00:00:30.150 --> 00:00:31.800
It's strange, though.

00:00:31.800 --> 00:00:34.980
It was just a four-bar idea 
that she'd hummed in the bath.

00:00:34.980 --> 00:00:37.550
She turned it into eight with Kyo's advice.

00:00:37.550 --> 00:00:42.180
We changed up the mood a little 
and turned it into eight more.

00:00:43.380 --> 00:00:48.020
We combined those two into 
an eighteen bar melody.

00:00:48.020 --> 00:00:49.900
You mean sixteen.

00:00:53.060 --> 00:00:55.830
That should do it for the melody.

00:00:55.830 --> 00:00:58.570
Let's try coming up with a chord progression.

00:00:59.180 --> 00:01:01.080
A chord progression?

00:01:01.620 --> 00:01:05.210
I guess you haven't thought about 
it much since you're a drummer.

00:01:05.210 --> 00:01:08.460
Chords? You mean with the Cs and Ds?

00:01:08.460 --> 00:01:09.580
Yeah.

00:01:09.580 --> 00:01:15.050
I probably don't have to explain to 
you, but for example, this is a C.

00:01:17.460 --> 00:01:18.740
This is a D.

00:01:20.030 --> 00:01:22.950
And this one's a bit harder: an F.

00:01:26.580 --> 00:01:31.480
So we have to put these things on 
top of the melody Jun came up with.

00:01:32.740 --> 00:01:35.190
It sounds complicated.

00:01:36.590 --> 00:01:40.740
There are a few cliches that 
you have to be aware of.

00:01:40.740 --> 00:01:42.910
It is a bit of a pain.

00:01:43.450 --> 00:01:46.680
But you don't have to let it bog you down.

00:01:46.680 --> 00:01:51.090
Just try each one, and plug in 
whatever sounds good to you.

00:01:51.090 --> 00:01:53.250
O-Okay.

00:01:53.700 --> 00:01:59.220
I don't know if I'll do a good 
job, but I'll do my best.

00:02:02.510 --> 00:02:05.020
Huh? Jun's composing?

00:02:05.900 --> 00:02:10.400
So that's why I heard her 
plucking at the guitar.

00:02:10.400 --> 00:02:14.650
She asked me if I have anything she 
can used to record her humming.

00:02:14.650 --> 00:02:17.030
I turned my closet upside 
down looking for one.

00:02:17.030 --> 00:02:18.530
Yeah, huh?

00:02:18.530 --> 00:02:20.780
Jun a composer, huh?

00:02:20.780 --> 00:02:23.230
It's <i>Jun's</i> research project.

00:02:23.230 --> 00:02:25.550
Don't get too involved.

00:02:30.000 --> 00:02:31.820
Come on.

00:02:31.820 --> 00:02:37.630
You could have told me. They used to 
call me the One-Man Glimmer Twins.

00:02:40.100 --> 00:02:41.760
I think G sounds good.

00:02:41.760 --> 00:02:43.750
This one's definitely a G.

00:02:43.750 --> 00:02:45.100
Want to try some other ones?

00:02:45.100 --> 00:02:48.990
No, I think G's perfect here.

00:02:48.990 --> 00:02:52.670
I think I'll try a C next.

00:02:57.410 --> 00:03:00.030
It's not bad, but...

00:03:00.360 --> 00:03:04.130
Maybe it would be more interesting 
with a little more of a twist.

00:03:04.130 --> 00:03:06.040
Let me try something.

00:03:11.620 --> 00:03:12.920
I like that.

00:03:14.820 --> 00:03:18.380
We went from a G to a D, and then 
maybe it's an E minor next?

00:03:25.510 --> 00:03:27.500
She doesn't need me.

00:03:29.130 --> 00:03:35.020
Kids sure do grow up before you know it.

00:03:56.010 --> 00:03:57.050
What do you think?

00:03:57.050 --> 00:04:01.740
I was thinking I'll add your piano 
to this, and we can call it done.

00:04:02.870 --> 00:04:05.420
Yeah. I think it's good.

00:04:06.670 --> 00:04:07.930
But...

00:04:08.630 --> 00:04:09.560
But?

00:04:10.430 --> 00:04:12.880
No, it's good.

00:04:12.880 --> 00:04:16.230
You made it for me, so I'll give it a try.

00:04:16.730 --> 00:04:17.860
Wait.

00:04:18.370 --> 00:04:21.180
Tell me if you aren't satisfied.

00:04:21.180 --> 00:04:24.240
I want to know what you want me to do.

00:04:24.900 --> 00:04:28.710
I don't know how it's going to end, 
but it's your first time on the stage.

00:04:28.710 --> 00:04:30.730
I want to do everything I can.

00:04:33.310 --> 00:04:34.770
Onii-chan...

00:04:36.780 --> 00:04:38.210
Don't try to be so cool.

00:04:40.930 --> 00:04:44.070
But thanks.

00:05:06.450 --> 00:05:09.200
H-How was it?

00:05:09.990 --> 00:05:14.210
What would you do if I 
told you to start over?

00:05:23.510 --> 00:05:29.970
Kyo-san, it might be wrong, 
but this is what I like.

00:05:30.350 --> 00:05:33.780
I want to finish the song 
with this chord progression.

00:05:36.340 --> 00:05:39.120
If you don't want to change it 
even after what I just said,

00:05:39.120 --> 00:05:41.970
then this is the right choice for you.

00:05:42.510 --> 00:05:43.610
Let's go with this.

00:05:45.330 --> 00:05:46.150
Okay.

00:06:02.380 --> 00:06:04.090
What do you think?

00:06:04.400 --> 00:06:05.770
I like it.

00:06:05.770 --> 00:06:09.070
It makes me eager to sing it.

00:06:10.050 --> 00:06:12.260
It's so-so.

00:06:12.260 --> 00:06:13.770
Hey!

00:06:13.770 --> 00:06:18.640
My brother made this at 
<i>my</i> request, for <i>my</i> sake.

00:06:18.640 --> 00:06:25.400
My, Hibiki was kind enough to listen to 
the pesky in-law for the sake of <i>my</i> band.

00:06:26.110 --> 00:06:26.940
How dare you!

00:06:27.290 --> 00:06:28.130
What?

00:06:28.130 --> 00:06:29.820
Are you angry because I'm right?

00:06:29.820 --> 00:06:31.910
This is getting exciting!

00:06:31.910 --> 00:06:34.820
That's what I want to see in a woman's fight!

00:06:34.820 --> 00:06:36.830
Please...

00:06:44.940 --> 00:06:47.000
If you want to change it up even more,

00:06:47.000 --> 00:06:50.470
you could start Melody B with a minor chord.

00:06:50.850 --> 00:06:52.550
I could.

00:06:53.430 --> 00:06:57.450
But I want to keep it happy this time.

00:06:58.090 --> 00:07:01.600
I'm always troubled and hesitant.

00:07:01.960 --> 00:07:05.480
I've always been bad at 
taking a step forward.

00:07:05.480 --> 00:07:07.580
That's why I want this song—

00:07:08.490 --> 00:07:13.870
my first song—to be a straightforward 
one with no hesitation.

00:07:15.550 --> 00:07:16.870
All right.

00:07:16.870 --> 00:07:19.370
Then let's flesh out the arrangement, and...

00:07:20.290 --> 00:07:22.390
We <i>still</i> can't play it?

00:07:23.100 --> 00:07:26.460
I want to play Jun-tan's song.

00:07:26.460 --> 00:07:28.020
You're right.

00:07:28.020 --> 00:07:33.760
I can't wait to hear what it'll sound like 
when we all play Jun's song together.

00:07:33.760 --> 00:07:35.350
Then...

00:07:36.230 --> 00:07:37.600
Can we, Jun?

00:07:37.600 --> 00:07:41.690
Yes, I want to play together, too.

00:07:48.330 --> 00:07:49.190
Okay.

00:07:49.190 --> 00:07:51.540
It's our big first take.

00:07:51.540 --> 00:07:52.910
Let's do it.

00:07:52.910 --> 00:07:54.240
Okay.

00:08:35.980 --> 00:08:36.990
Well...

00:08:37.460 --> 00:08:38.750
It's a good song.

00:08:59.610 --> 00:09:01.810
Jun-tan's struggling.

00:09:02.410 --> 00:09:04.370
She went into the bath saying it 
might help her come up with lyrics,

00:09:04.370 --> 00:09:07.100
like it did when she was humming.

00:09:07.100 --> 00:09:08.940
It's been a while now.

00:09:08.940 --> 00:09:10.820
I hope she's okay.

00:09:11.690 --> 00:09:12.450
Wait, Jun!

00:09:12.450 --> 00:09:13.690
Jun-tan!

00:09:14.790 --> 00:09:15.700
Jeez.

00:09:15.700 --> 00:09:17.700
You didn't have to stay in 
the bath until you passed out,

00:09:17.700 --> 00:09:20.210
just because you're having 
trouble with the lyrics.

00:09:21.200 --> 00:09:25.120
You could have been in trouble 
if we weren't peeping.

00:09:26.030 --> 00:09:29.000
Sorry, Zomi, Ku-chan.

00:09:30.140 --> 00:09:33.920
Hey, if it's okay with you, can we help out?

00:09:33.920 --> 00:09:36.630
Like the time the three 
of us composed together.

00:09:37.870 --> 00:09:44.180
Thanks, but I decided I 
would do this by myself.

00:09:45.100 --> 00:09:46.410
You're right.

00:09:46.410 --> 00:09:48.860
You said you'd take on the challenge,

00:09:48.860 --> 00:09:51.050
even if you aren't sure 
you can do a good job.

00:09:52.050 --> 00:09:54.630
That's the policy at Little Wing.

00:09:54.630 --> 00:09:56.570
Since when?

00:09:56.570 --> 00:10:00.200
Since Jun-tan said 
we should start a band.

00:10:09.430 --> 00:10:12.960
Are you sure you needed to buy a keyboard?

00:10:12.960 --> 00:10:14.200
It's fine.

00:10:14.200 --> 00:10:16.100
I bought it with my own savings.

00:10:16.100 --> 00:10:18.170
I won't let anyone complain.

00:10:18.740 --> 00:10:21.600
But we have an electronic piano at home.

00:10:22.030 --> 00:10:23.930
That thing's heavy.

00:10:23.930 --> 00:10:27.350
It'll be hard to carry it back 
and forth for the concert.

00:10:28.350 --> 00:10:29.770
Back and forth?

00:10:30.300 --> 00:10:34.440
N-Not that I've decided 
to keep playing with <i>her</i>.

00:10:34.440 --> 00:10:38.950
But I thought it might not be a bad 
idea to keep doing music with someone.

00:10:41.390 --> 00:10:42.990
Want me to carry that?

00:10:42.990 --> 00:10:45.200
No, I'll carry it.

00:10:45.200 --> 00:10:47.970
It's my instrument.

00:11:00.590 --> 00:11:04.600
Slipped and fell in a puddle of tears
Afraid of the end of night
About to disappear
But even those footsteps...

00:11:14.370 --> 00:11:18.630
Are you sure you want to be fishing 
with me right before the concert?

00:11:19.390 --> 00:11:21.130
Practicing is important,

00:11:21.130 --> 00:11:25.120
but it's not good to hurt your fingers 
or strings practicing too hard, either.

00:11:25.120 --> 00:11:30.370
Besides, Jun said she wanted to focus 
on writing lyrics for the new song.

00:11:30.860 --> 00:11:33.500
So we're taking the day off from practice.

00:11:33.500 --> 00:11:35.250
Yeah, huh?

00:11:36.590 --> 00:11:41.080
You didn't have to come hang out with 
me so early in the morning, though.

00:11:41.080 --> 00:11:43.000
I had to.

00:11:43.000 --> 00:11:47.000
You've helped me out preparing 
for the concert and stuff.

00:11:47.000 --> 00:11:48.770
I wanted to pay you back a little.

00:11:51.490 --> 00:11:53.920
We aren't strangers or anything.

00:11:53.920 --> 00:11:56.980
We're practically family.

00:11:57.740 --> 00:12:01.940
I mean, I don't mean that like I want 
to become a real family with you

00:12:01.940 --> 00:12:03.430
eventually or anything.

00:12:05.380 --> 00:12:06.120
It's tugging.

00:12:06.970 --> 00:12:07.720
There.

00:12:07.720 --> 00:12:08.830
Hurry!

00:12:11.410 --> 00:12:11.960
Reel it in!

00:12:12.350 --> 00:12:13.540
You have to pull it up!

00:12:13.540 --> 00:12:14.170
Come on!

00:12:14.170 --> 00:12:14.880
Hey!

00:12:29.470 --> 00:12:31.980
I'll make it to the sound I admire someday
It's time to jam, believe in the first take
I slipped and fell in a puddle of tears
Shoes covered in mud, world blurry again
Afraid of the end of the night
I can't even be happy about the beginning of the day, I'm going to disappear
But those footsteps in retrospect turn out to be precious memories
Because the mark that I reached today when I jumped
Compared to the spot I reached yesterday
Was a bit more of a high jump
I'll make it to the sound I admire someday
It's time to jam, believe in the first take

00:12:31.090 --> 00:12:31.980
Um...

00:12:31.980 --> 00:12:34.580
Are these lyrics okay?

00:12:35.190 --> 00:12:36.930
There's no good or bad.

00:12:38.180 --> 00:12:41.410
If this is what you want 
to sing, it's correct.

00:12:41.840 --> 00:12:44.860
This is your song, after all.

00:12:47.350 --> 00:12:49.370
But we have to choose a title.

00:12:49.370 --> 00:12:51.930
I've already chosen a title.

00:12:53.250 --> 00:12:55.380
It's "First Take."

00:13:06.100 --> 00:13:08.140
You don't need that anymore, do you?

00:13:11.140 --> 00:13:12.980
You noticed?

00:13:12.980 --> 00:13:14.640
Of course I did.

00:13:14.950 --> 00:13:20.000
Jun—the kids—can face 
forward when they sing now.

00:13:20.000 --> 00:13:21.400
Powerfully.

00:13:23.620 --> 00:13:26.570
Kyo, it's all thanks to you.

00:13:34.290 --> 00:13:36.790
<b>Little Wing
Live
Keyboard & Vocals: Goto Jun
Bass: Momijidani Nozomi
Drums: Kaneshiro Sora</b>

00:13:42.300 --> 00:13:45.470
"We have a special guest today.

00:13:45.470 --> 00:13:50.040
Please vote for whether you liked 
Lien de Famille or the guest."

00:13:50.040 --> 00:13:54.020
But the audience is here 
to see Lien de Famille.

00:13:54.020 --> 00:13:56.230
The guest's got a huge disadvantage.

00:13:56.930 --> 00:13:59.340
You don't get it, Mizuno.

00:13:59.340 --> 00:14:02.360
That's why it's worth doing.

00:14:02.360 --> 00:14:06.240
It doesn't make sense that you're 
getting so pumped, Isurugi.

00:14:32.460 --> 00:14:35.350
Welcome to Live House Little Wing.

00:14:45.170 --> 00:14:48.250
You'd better not be freaking out <i>now</i>.

00:14:48.250 --> 00:14:49.010
What?

00:14:49.010 --> 00:14:50.580
Of course not.

00:14:51.320 --> 00:14:53.410
This is our first performance.

00:14:53.410 --> 00:14:55.200
Let's give it our best.

00:14:56.950 --> 00:15:01.080
Let's show them how awesome we are.

00:15:05.490 --> 00:15:06.840
Yeah.

00:15:08.860 --> 00:15:09.700
Yes.

00:15:30.610 --> 00:15:32.920
Nice to meet you, everyone.

00:15:32.920 --> 00:15:34.230
We are...

00:15:34.230 --> 00:15:39.010
Wait, we haven't come up with 
a name for our band, have we?

00:15:42.410 --> 00:15:43.730
Um...

00:15:43.730 --> 00:15:49.170
We don't have a name yet, but I hope 
you give us a little bit of your time.

00:15:56.850 --> 00:16:09.940
<i>Hear the glimmering</i>

00:16:09.940 --> 00:16:24.390
<i>I wanted to embrace you 
like a warm bowl of soup</i>

00:16:25.210 --> 00:16:32.460
<i>It turned out, you felt the same way</i>

00:16:32.460 --> 00:16:38.350
<i>I was surprised, but even more, I was happy</i>

00:16:38.350 --> 00:16:45.750
<i>You can't help but smile</i>

00:16:45.750 --> 00:16:54.780
<i>The treasure I'd been looking 
for was right here all along</i>

00:16:54.780 --> 00:17:02.410
<i>My love for you will never die, 
whether you cry or become stubborn</i>

00:17:02.410 --> 00:17:18.660
<i>Listen carefully, and you'll
hear the invisible treasure</i>

00:17:40.170 --> 00:17:44.860
We're not going to be 
outdone in the second half.

00:17:45.310 --> 00:17:47.230
This is our first time 
playing this next song.

00:17:47.230 --> 00:17:50.250
It's called "First Take."

00:17:51.420 --> 00:17:53.920
Jun-tan worked hard to write it.

00:17:56.900 --> 00:18:01.650
And it's the song we want 
to play for you the most.

00:18:07.860 --> 00:18:15.290
<i>I'll make it to the sound I admire someday</i>

00:18:15.290 --> 00:18:24.350
<i>It's time to jam, believe in the first take</i>

00:18:28.430 --> 00:18:35.090
<i>I slipped and fell in a puddle of tears</i>

00:18:35.090 --> 00:18:41.720
<i>Shoes covered in mud, world blurry again</i>

00:18:41.720 --> 00:18:45.620
<i>Afraid of the end of the night</i>

00:18:45.620 --> 00:18:54.730
<i>I can't even be happy about the beginning 
of the day, I'm going to disappear</i>

00:18:54.730 --> 00:19:08.200
<i>But those footsteps in retrospect 
turn out to be precious memories</i>

00:19:08.200 --> 00:19:12.550
<i>Because the mark that I
reached today when I jumped</i>

00:19:12.550 --> 00:19:16.750
<i>Compared to the spot I reached yesterday</i>

00:19:16.750 --> 00:19:21.690
<i>Was a bit more of a high jump</i>

00:19:21.690 --> 00:19:29.020
<i>I'll make it to the sound I admire someday</i>

00:19:29.020 --> 00:19:38.090
<i>It's time to jam, believe in the first take</i>

00:20:23.780 --> 00:20:26.240
<b>Lien
de Famille</b>

00:20:26.240 --> 00:20:28.790
<b>Homewrecker
Dragon Sisters
(tentative)</b>

00:20:27.460 --> 00:20:30.950
Looks like we lost, Kiryu-sama.

00:20:30.950 --> 00:20:33.530
Well, we did all we could.

00:20:33.530 --> 00:20:34.330
Huh?

00:20:34.330 --> 00:20:36.420
You aren't angry that you lost?

00:20:36.420 --> 00:20:39.310
We're totally the away team.

00:20:39.310 --> 00:20:41.420
I'm glad we got this many.

00:20:41.420 --> 00:20:44.680
You could say that was our greeting jab.

00:20:44.680 --> 00:20:47.180
We're still doing more?

00:20:47.180 --> 00:20:51.180
I never thought you'd draw for Jun and them.

00:20:51.580 --> 00:20:52.760
I know.

00:20:52.760 --> 00:20:56.380
And I never even told you about our song.

00:20:56.380 --> 00:20:57.900
How did you come up with that drawing?

00:20:57.900 --> 00:20:59.550
What could I do?

00:20:59.550 --> 00:21:01.730
It just came to me.

00:21:02.910 --> 00:21:06.530
Are we connected to you now, Kiriyume?

00:21:06.530 --> 00:21:09.120
Don't be crazy!

00:21:09.120 --> 00:21:12.000
I only need to be connected to Hibiki.

00:21:13.300 --> 00:21:14.810
L-Let's go.

00:21:14.810 --> 00:21:16.010
Okay.

00:21:18.190 --> 00:21:21.170
Kurumi, you're on our side.

00:21:21.170 --> 00:21:22.420
Hurry up.

00:21:22.420 --> 00:21:25.020
Fine, fine, I got it.

00:21:25.020 --> 00:21:26.380
Koume-chan.

00:21:26.380 --> 00:21:28.390
Stop calling me Koume-chan!

00:21:28.390 --> 00:21:30.030
You're so stubborn.

00:21:30.030 --> 00:21:31.020
She's right.

00:21:31.020 --> 00:21:33.890
You're so stubborn, Koume-chan.

00:21:33.890 --> 00:21:35.090
You, too, Yuzuha?

00:21:35.090 --> 00:21:36.390
Stop saying Koume-chan!

00:21:39.250 --> 00:21:40.650
Stop saying Koume-chan!

00:21:40.650 --> 00:21:41.620
Um...

00:21:41.620 --> 00:21:43.070
What is it?

00:21:43.070 --> 00:21:47.100
Nothing, I was just thinking...

00:21:56.170 --> 00:22:00.350
that nothing beats music.

00:22:04.170 --> 00:22:08.010
<b>Can't Help but 
Love the Music</b>
